  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Separate authoritative owners",
      "items": [
        "Gateway Registry owns grants, immutable operation correlation, execution reservations and durable CLI-routing permits. Observations are dated caches; Native alone owns task admission, launch, supervision and accepted outcomes.",
        "Connector owns immutable local alias pins and a stricter provider/permission/budget ceiling. Effective execution rights require both current Gateway grants and the local ceiling; no automatic repin or failover.",
        "Schema 7 keeps routing permits separate from task reservations. CLI Wait/cleanup, definite non-publication or fenced same-process census can settle routing; only canonical task closure, matching confirmed stop or permanent refusal settles transmitted execution uncertainty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust, fleet coverage and joins",
      "items": [
        "Separate TLS 1.3 listeners: public HTTPS OAuth/JWKS MCP and device mTLS WSS. Each connector initiates outbound WSS; Gateway sees plaintext. Two device roles illustrate topology, not physical-device/network acceptance.",
        "Complete prior-fleet routing coverage precedes ANY routed CLI, including protected recovery controls. Changed process identity needs explicit out-of-band frozen local CLI-join attestation bound to current credential, process boot and exact connection generation.",
        "Connector census/ACK gates claims. Accepted controls retain ownership through actual Wait and cleanup; timeout/socket closure never proves task closure. Phase-4 schema-7 compaction deletes only closed older routing rows, never active controls or task evidence.",
        "Same account is a trusted device boundary. Project grants route requests; they are not an OS sandbox. Native CLI is a separately reviewed prerequisite, not an embedded second engine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Source-backed candidate, bounded evidence",
      "items": [
        "Gateway source is pinned to commit 5e065e84 (full revision in metadata). All node references resolve against committed Gateway bytes with local-only links. External Native nodes cite the Gateway consumer contract, not foreign implementation.",
        "Native is an external prerequisite: namespace-admission-v1 and namespace-mutation-lease-v1 are both required. The reviewed Native prerequisite is commit 62b11d34 (PR 179); an arbitrary installed CLI is not presumed compatible.",
        "Gateway enforces frozen task guards, root-only namespace probes and live project checks for new execution. Current commands, results and remaining acceptance limits belong in docs/verification.md; this diagram supplies source provenance, not runtime or release proof."
      ]
    }
  ]
